entations"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Progression"},{"type":"h","text":"0–2 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Intern","Research Assistant","Policy Research Associate"]},{"type":"h","text":"2–5 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Policy Researcher","Policy Analyst","Defence/Strategic Affairs Analyst"]},{"type":"h","text":"5–8 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Senior Policy Analyst","Research Fellow","Strategic Affairs Specialist"]},{"type":"h","text":"8+ years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Senior Research Fellow","Programme Director","Research/Policy Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best overall strategy"},{"type":"p","text":"For a BA Defence & Strategic Studies → Policy Researcher pathway, the strongest profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Defence & Strategic Studies","Research Methods","Geopolitics","Policy Analysis","Data Analytics","OSINT","Strategic Technology"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The degree provides the strategic foundation, but employability comes from being able to turn complex security and geopolitical questions into credible evidence, structured analysis, clear policy options, and concise recommendations. A master's in Strategic Studies, International Security, International Relations, Defence Studies, or Public Policy is particularly valuable for advancing into specialised policy-research roles."}]}]}